[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Training Elephants]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.60]Lesson 41 | 第41课
[00:02.75]Training elephants | 训练大象
[00:10.54]At what point does the training of a captive wild elephant begin? | 对捕获的野象的训练从什么时候开始？
[00:17.74]Two main techniques have been used for training elephants, which we may call respectively the tough and the gentle. | 训练大象历来主要有两种方法，我们不妨分别叫作强硬法和温柔法。
[00:27.25]The former method simply consists of setting an elephant to work and beating him until he does what is expected of him. | 前一种方法只是叫大象去干活，打到它按人的要求去做为止。
[00:36.67]Apart from any moral considerations this is a stupid method of training, | 且不说任何道德方面的考虑，这是一种愚蠢的训练方法，
[00:42.29]for it produces a resentful animal who at a later stage may well turn man-killer. | 因为它训练出的是一头心怀怨恨的动物，日后很可能会变成伤人的象。
[00:49.31]The gentle method requires more patience in the early stages, | 温柔法在初期需要更多的耐心，
[00:53.72]but produce a cheerful good-tempered elephant who will give many years of loyal service. | 但培养出一头快活、脾气好的象，它将提供多年忠诚的服务。
[01:01.86]The first essential in elephant training is to assign to the animal a single mahout who will be entirely responsible for the job. | 训练大象的首要之点是给象指定一名驯象员，由他全权负责这项工作。
[01:12.02]Elephants like to have one master just as dogs do, and are capable of a considerable degree of personal affection. | 象和狗一样喜欢有一个主人，能够有相当程度的依恋之情。
[01:21.71]There are even stories of half-trained elephant calves who have refused to feed and pined to death | 甚至有这样的故事：训练到一半的幼象在被夺走自己的驯象员之后
[01:30.54]when by some unavoidable circumstance they have been deprived of their own trainer. | 由于某种无法避免的情况而拒食并憔悴致死。
[01:38.41]Such extreme cases must probably be taken with a grain of salt, | 这样的极端事例也许得打折扣听，
[01:43.26]but they do underline the general principle that the relationship between elephant and mahout is the key to successful training. | 但它们确实强调了总原则：象与驯象员的关系是训练成功的关键。
[01:54.24]The most economical age to capture an elephant for training is between 15 and 20 years, | 捕象训练的最经济年龄在15岁到20岁之间，
[02:01.53]for it is then almost ready to undertake heavy work and can begin to earn its keep straight away. | 因为那时它几乎能承担重活，并能马上开始挣回饲料钱。
[02:09.29]But animals of this age do not easily become subservient to man, and a very firm hand must be employed in the early stages. | 但这个年龄的动物不容易驯服于人，初期必须使用非常强硬的手段。
[02:19.42]The captive elephant, still roped to a tree, | 捕获的象仍被拴在树上时，
[02:22.74]plunges and screams every time a man approaches, and for several days will probably refuse all food through anger and fear. | 每当有人走近，它就又冲又叫，而且由于愤怒和恐惧，很可能会连续几天拒绝进食。
[02:34.27]Sometimes a tame elephant is tethered nearby to give the wild one confidence, | 有时把一头驯服的象拴在附近，给野象以信心，
[02:40.27]and in most cases the captive gradually quietens down and begins to accept its food. | 在大多数情况下，捕获的象会渐渐安静下来，开始接受食物。
[02:47.81]The next stage is to get the elephant to the training establishment, | 下一步是把象带到训练场，
[02:51.87]a ticklish business which is achieved with the aid of two tame elephants roped to the captive on either side. | 这是一件棘手的事，靠两头驯象拴在捕获的象两侧来完成。
[02:59.97]When several elephants are being trained at one time, | 当一次训练几头象时，
[03:04.05]it is customary for the new arrival to be placed between the stalls of two captives whose training is already well advanced. | 通常把新来的象安置在两头训练已大有进展的捕获象的栏位之间。
[03:13.88]It is then left completely undisturbed with plenty of food and water | 然后让它完全不受打扰，并给予充足的食物和水，
[03:19.15]so that it can absorb the atmosphere of its new home and see that nothing particularly alarming is happening to its companions. | 以使它能够适应新家的气氛，并看到同伴们并没有遭遇什么特别可怕的事情。
[03:28.39]When it is eating normally, its own training begins. | 当它正常进食后，对它本身的训练便开始了。
[03:33.27]The trainer stands in front of the elephant holding a long stick with a sharp metal point. | 驯象员站在象的前面，手拿一根带金属尖头的长棍。
[03:39.70]Two assistants, mounted on tame elephants, control the captive from either side, | 两名助手骑在驯服的象背上，从两侧控制这头捕获的象，
[03:46.63]while others rub their hands over his skin to the accompaniment of a monotonous and soothing chant. | 其余的人则在他的皮肤上摩挲双手，同时伴以单调而舒缓的吟唱。
[03:55.06]This is supposed to induce pleasurable sensations in the elephant, | 这被认为能给象带来愉快的感觉，
[03:59.73]and its effects are reinforced by the use of endearing epithets, | 这种效果又因使用亲昵的称呼而得到加强，
[04:03.69]such as 'ho! my son', or 'ho! my father', or 'my mother', according to the age and sex of the captive. | 比如“嗬！我的儿子”，或“嗬！我的父亲”，或“我的母亲”，视捕获象的年龄和性别而定。
[04:15.71]The elephant is not immediately susceptible to such blandishments, however, and usually lashes fiercely with its trunk in all directions. | 然而，象不会立刻被这种甜言蜜语所打动，通常会用鼻子朝四面八方凶猛地抽打。
[04:25.47]These movements are controlled by the trainer with the metal-pointed stick, | 这些动作被驯象员用带金属尖头的棍子所控制，
[04:30.01]and the trunk eventually becomes so sore that the elephant curls it up and seldom afterwards uses it for offensive purposes. | 鼻子最终变得如此疼痛，以至于象把它卷了起来，此后极少再用它去进攻。
